1308
01:24:01,570 --> 01:24:03,106
Bullshit. Show me.

1309
01:24:07,643 --> 01:24:09,412
Oh, oh no.

1310
01:24:09,578 --> 01:24:11,780
Did your letter get wet?
It's ruined it, hasn't it?

1311
01:24:11,947 --> 01:24:13,316
Oh, what a pity.

1312
01:24:13,482 --> 01:24:15,584
You see, what we actually
have here

1313
01:24:15,751 --> 01:24:18,521
is called force majeure, which
is an unforeseen natural act.

1314
01:24:18,687 --> 01:24:22,258
And guess what? That absolves me
of all responsibility.

1315
01:24:22,425 --> 01:24:23,659
Sorry!

1316
01:24:24,593 --> 01:24:27,196
I've got copies of everything.
I'll help you.

1317
01:24:27,763 --> 01:24:29,098
Rachel. What are you doing?

1318
01:24:29,265 --> 01:24:31,367
I've been helping you for years.

1319
01:24:31,534 --> 01:24:33,536
Hiding your mistakes.
Covering up your fuckups.

1320
01:24:33,702 --> 01:24:34,803
Yeah, it's your job!

1321
01:24:34,970 --> 01:24:36,339
Well, you're a disgusting
human being

1322
01:24:36,505 --> 01:24:37,706
and I despise you.

1323
01:24:37,873 --> 01:24:39,208
You cannot talk to me like that.

1324
01:24:39,375 --> 01:24:41,043
You're an Infinity
Dream employee.

1325
01:24:41,210 --> 01:24:43,212
Well, do you want to shove
this up your arse?

1326
01:24:43,379 --> 01:24:44,947
Or shall I do it for you?

1327
01:24:45,114 --> 01:24:46,482
Alright, very good.

1328
01:24:49,718 --> 01:24:50,786
Ow!

1329
01:24:51,654 --> 01:24:53,156
Right, I've had enough of this.

1330
01:24:53,789 --> 01:24:55,358
You're not gonna make it!

1331
01:24:55,524 --> 01:24:56,559
Watch me!

1332
01:24:56,725 --> 01:24:58,361
The tides are too strong!

1333
01:24:58,527 --> 01:25:00,796
For you, because you're weak!

1334
01:25:00,963 --> 01:25:05,134
In fact, your whole, your whole
generation is weak!

1335
01:25:05,301 --> 01:25:09,205
You're weak, lazy,
self-obsessed!

1336
01:25:09,538 --> 01:25:13,742
In fact, you are...
you're so, so self-obsessed,

1337
01:25:13,909 --> 01:25:18,814
you literally think that work
is photographing your food

1338
01:25:18,981 --> 01:25:23,051
and sharing every magnificent
bubble-headed thought

1339
01:25:23,219 --> 01:25:25,188
that comes into your head!

1340
01:25:26,222 --> 01:25:29,192
You're not, you know what?
You're not Gen Z.

1341
01:25:29,358 --> 01:25:32,595
You're genpanzee!
You're pathetic!

1342
01:25:32,761 --> 01:25:34,197
See ya!

1343
01:25:34,363 --> 01:25:35,731
Fuck off!

1344
01:25:35,898 --> 01:25:38,167
My generation is trying
to find their way

1345
01:25:38,334 --> 01:25:40,369
because your generation
fucked up everything.

1346
01:25:40,536 --> 01:25:42,405
And now nature's biting you
in the arse

1347
01:25:42,571 --> 01:25:43,772
and you don't like it!

1348
01:25:43,939 --> 01:25:45,107
Yeah, yeah.

1349
01:25:45,274 --> 01:25:47,210
Nothing's biting me!

1350
01:25:47,376 --> 01:25:49,612
Spiders can't swim!

1351
01:25:49,878 --> 01:25:52,181
Ooh!

1352
01:25:52,348 --> 01:25:53,282
Uh!

1353
01:26:02,258 --> 01:26:03,859
Rachel, help!

1354
01:26:04,026 --> 01:26:05,961
No! Aaargh!

1355
01:26:09,698 --> 01:26:10,733
No!

1356
01:26:10,899 --> 01:26:12,067
Rachel!

1357
01:26:12,235 --> 01:26:13,302
Aargh!

1358
01:26:19,542 --> 01:26:22,378
Well, I wasn't expecting that.

1359
01:26:23,912 --> 01:26:25,113
No.

1360
01:26:25,614 --> 01:26:28,617
I mean, that captain fella,
he said there were sharks.

1361
01:26:33,756 --> 01:26:35,123
I got signal!

1362
01:26:35,291 --> 01:26:36,525
Me too.

1363
01:26:37,260 --> 01:26:39,228
I'll call Captain Brunner
and let him know where we are.

1364
01:26:44,833 --> 01:26:46,835
How the hell
is that dog still alive?

1365
01:26:47,470 --> 01:26:50,339
No, how the hell
is he still alive?

1366
01:26:51,974 --> 01:26:53,309
I'm alright!

1367
01:26:54,310 --> 01:26:55,511
I'm alright!

1368
01:26:58,581 --> 01:26:59,748
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

1369
01:26:59,915 --> 01:27:01,817
It's okay, it's okay.

1370
01:27:02,150 --> 01:27:05,020
They're just...
riding along, you know,

1371
01:27:05,187 --> 01:27:07,756
having the occasional nibble,
but I'm alright.

1372
01:27:08,090 --> 01:27:09,958
They're just really
beautiful animals.

1373
01:27:10,125 --> 01:27:11,794
q

1374
01:27:11,960 --> 01:27:13,996
No!

1375
01:27:14,162 --> 01:27:16,532
That's not very
respectful to nature.

1376
01:27:16,699 --> 01:27:19,668
Aargh! Aargh! Die!

1377
01:27:21,770 --> 01:27:23,706
She's killing my friends.

1378
01:27:26,809 --> 01:27:28,711
How are you not dead?

1379
01:27:29,211 --> 01:27:31,514
Well, aside from being
an absolute legend

1380
01:27:31,680 --> 01:27:34,817
with an amazing capacity
for drugs, I'd say...

1381
01:27:36,084 --> 01:27:37,886
The venom of the cane toad
protects you

1382
01:27:38,053 --> 01:27:39,622
from the poison of the spiders.

1383
01:27:39,788 --> 01:27:41,624
Either that
or I'm a really lucky git.

1384
01:27:45,961 --> 01:27:48,531
Did you lick a cane toad
with my dad by any chance?

1385
01:27:48,997 --> 01:27:51,033
Oh yeah. The old guy,
the actor fella

1386
01:27:51,199 --> 01:27:52,401
with the really shitty bar?

1387
01:27:52,635 --> 01:27:54,036
I must say, he was...

1388
01:27:55,137 --> 01:27:56,872
Really partial to a lick.

1389
01:28:11,554 --> 01:28:12,688
Dad?

1390
01:28:15,691 --> 01:28:16,925
Dad?!

1391
01:28:17,426 --> 01:28:18,527
Dad?

1392
01:28:21,764 --> 01:28:23,031
Dad!!

1393
01:28:26,435 --> 01:28:27,736
Dad?!

1394
01:28:32,708 --> 01:28:34,076
Dad?!

1395
01:29:37,673 --> 01:29:39,808
My darling Clara.

1396
01:29:39,975 --> 01:29:41,744
I hope you are reading this
as a woman

1397
01:29:41,910 --> 01:29:43,846
and that you're happy
in your life.

1398
01:29:44,279 --> 01:29:46,582
I hope you can bring yourself
to forgive me

1399
01:29:46,749 --> 01:29:49,452
for taking you away
from this beautiful island.

1400
01:29:51,153 --> 01:29:52,821
We tried to make
the marriage work,

1401
01:29:52,988 --> 01:29:55,123
but your dad cared so much
about saving the planet,

1402
01:29:55,290 --> 01:29:57,192
there wasn't much time
for anything else.

1403
01:29:57,426 --> 01:30:00,328
I know that sounds a bit
heartless, but it's the truth.

1404
01:30:04,166 --> 01:30:06,168
Life stopped being fun,

1405
01:30:06,334 --> 01:30:08,504
and life should never
not be fun.

1406
01:30:08,837 --> 01:30:11,640
To die, to sleep.

1407
01:30:11,807 --> 01:30:14,810
No more, and by a sleep

1408
01:30:14,977 --> 01:30:18,146
to say we end the heartache

1409
01:30:18,346 --> 01:30:22,951
and the thousand natural shocks
that flesh is heir to.

1410
01:30:24,386 --> 01:30:27,623
'Tis a consummation
devoutly to be wished.

1411
01:30:27,990 --> 01:30:30,826
To die, to sleep.

1412
01:30:30,993 --> 01:30:32,294
Dad?

1413
01:30:33,328 --> 01:30:35,030
To sleep...

1414
01:30:36,565 --> 01:30:38,233
perchance to dream.

1415
01:30:38,400 --> 01:30:42,037
Aye, there's the rub.
For in that sleep of death,

1416
01:30:42,204 --> 01:30:44,873
what dreams may come
when we have shuffled off

1417
01:30:45,040 --> 01:30:48,644
